/*!
    \qmltype GameplayContext
    \inqmlmodule RhythmGameQml
    \brief Supplies play data to decide and gameplay screens.

    Declare \c {required property GameplayContext gameplay} on the screen root.
    The game supplies the object when it creates decide and passes the same
    object to gameplay. Every gameplay theme must support single charts and courses.

    Bind to the current chart and players so the display follows course stages.
    Don't keep using a Player from an earlier stage. The context only supplies
    data. Pass it to StandardDecideFlow::gameplay or StandardGameplayFlow::gameplay
    to use the standard input and transitions.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty ChartData GameplayContext::chartData
    \readonly
    Describes the current chart. It keeps the last stage after the course finishes.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty list<Player> GameplayContext::players
    \readonly
    Contains one Player for solo or double play, or two for local battle.
    Each player supplies a profile, notes, state, live score and timing.
    There is no null second entry in solo play. The list and chart metadata
    update together after the next course stage has been installed.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty var GameplayContext::course
    \readonly
    Contains the course definition when isCourse is true. It is undefined for a single chart.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty bool GameplayContext::isCourse
    \readonly
    Reports whether the play is a course. Use it when adding course details
    to the display. The current chart uses the same interface in either case.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty bool GameplayContext::isArena
    \readonly
    Reports whether the play belongs to Arena. The game handles its startup and lifetime.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty list<ChartData> GameplayContext::charts
    \readonly
    Contains chart metadata in stage order. A single chart has one entry.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty int GameplayContext::stageIndex
    \readonly
    Gives the current stage index, starting at zero. It stays at the last stage after completion.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty int GameplayContext::stageCount
    \readonly
    Gives the number of stages. A single chart has one stage.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty list<CoursePlayer> GameplayContext::coursePlayers
    \readonly
    Contains combo state for the whole course, in player order. The list is empty for a single chart.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty var GameplayContext::bga
    \readonly
    Provides the current BGA container. It is initially null while the stage loads.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty int GameplayContext::status
    \readonly
    Reports the current stage status as ChartRunner.Loading, Ready, Running or Finished.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty int GameplayContext::keymode
    \readonly
    Gives the keymode used for play, including changes made by play options.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty list<int> GameplayContext::inputMapping
    Maps physical BMS input to the columns used by the theme's lane layout.
    The game checks the mapping and keeps it between course stages.
*/
/*!
    \qmltype ResultContext
    \inqmlmodule RhythmGameQml
    \brief Supplies a completed chart result, including a course stage.

    Declare \c {required property ResultContext result} on a normal result
    screen. The game supplies the completed chart and scores when it opens the
    screen. Chart metadata and totals stay fixed after a course advances,
    although online score submission state can still change.

    Bind the context to StandardResultInput::result for confirmation and
    supported single-chart retry. Read the result's own metadata when showing
    the completed stage, since the originating play may have advanced.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty ChartData ResultContext::chartData
    \readonly
    Describes the completed chart, regardless of the current gameplay stage.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty list<ResultPlayer> ResultContext::players
    \readonly
    Contains one or two ResultPlayer entries. Each pairs a profile with a completed BmsScore.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty GameplayContext ResultContext::gameplay
    \readonly
    Refers to the originating play, or null if the result was opened without one.
    Standard retry uses this reference. The play remains live and may describe
    the next stage, so use the result's chart and stage fields for the completed stage.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty string ResultContext::arenaRoundId
    \readonly
    Identifies the Arena round for this result. It is empty for local play and
    saved-score views. Standard gameplay supplies it before the screen is created,
    so a result screen doesn't need an initialization callback from the host.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty var ResultContext::course
    \readonly
    Contains the course definition for a stage result. It is undefined for a single chart.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty int ResultContext::stageIndex
    \readonly
    Gives the completed stage index, starting at zero. It stays fixed and is zero for a single chart.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty int ResultContext::stageCount
    \readonly
    Gives the stage count of the originating play. It stays fixed and is one for a single chart.
*/
/*!
    \qmltype ResultPlayer
    \inqmlmodule RhythmGameQml
    \brief Profile and score paired within a normal result.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty Profile ResultPlayer::profile
    \readonly
    Participant's profile.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty BmsScore ResultPlayer::score
    \readonly
    Completed chart score, including statistics, replay and gauge history.
*/
/*!
    \qmltype CourseResultContext
    \inqmlmodule RhythmGameQml
    \brief Completed course summary supplied to the course-result screen.

    Declare \c {required property CourseResultContext result} on a course result
    screen. The game selects the course result separately from the normal result.
    A theme can provide either role or both, with a separate contract for each.

    StandardResultInput can close a course summary. Single-chart retry is
    unavailable because the result describes the whole course.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty var CourseResultContext::course
    \readonly
    Completed course definition.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty list<ChartData> CourseResultContext::charts
    \readonly
    Contains the course charts in stage order.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty list<CourseResultPlayer> CourseResultContext::players
    \readonly
    Contains one or two CourseResultPlayer entries. Each pairs a profile with an aggregate course score.
*/
/*!
    \qmltype CourseResultPlayer
    \inqmlmodule RhythmGameQml
    \brief Profile and aggregate score paired within a course summary.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty Profile CourseResultPlayer::profile
    \readonly
    Participant's profile.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty BmsScoreCourse CourseResultPlayer::score
    \readonly
    Aggregate course score, including its individual stage scores.
*/

/*!
    \qmlproperty bool GameplayContext::arenaActive
    \readonly
    Reports whether the Arena session still presents this runner as its active
    gameplay. Use it for Arena targets and standings. It is independent of the
    theme's overlays and becomes false when play ends or the session releases the round.
*/
/*!
    \qmlproperty bool ResultContext::arenaActive
    \readonly
    Reports whether the Arena session still presents this result's round.
    Use it for standings and chat input rules, including in themes that draw
    their own panel. The context checks the round ID and session state, so the
    theme doesn't need to repeat those checks. Local results and saved scores
    return false.
*/
